# site/tour.html is the canonical record of the bytes served at
# gotovasl.com/tour. Its source is VASL-HEALTH/vasl-platform
# infra/aws/demo-site/content/portal-tour.html, which pins
# `content/*.html -text` for the same reason.
#
# The blob is LF. This repo sets core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF to
# CRLF on checkout, so without this pin a Windows working copy would be
# 22,537 bytes instead of 22,206 and a deploy from it would upload CRLF --
# same rendering, different Content-Length, and the repo copy would stop
# matching the live S3 object. With the pin, a checkout is byte-identical
# to the blob on every platform.
site/tour.html -text
